  "text_md": "Figure 1: Distribution of interpolation and evaluation nodes within a circle of radius 0.1.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nFigure 2: Comparison of Accuracy and Numerical Stability for HRBF and MHRBF: The errors (function; f , and its first derivatives; fr and fy) and condition number computed in double precision for GA kernel, as functions of shape parameter €, with polynomial degree of 6 and 4 for MHRBF\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nThe results in Figure 2 reveal significant accuracy improvements with MHRBF compared to HRBF . Since the error trends for Vf closely follow that of f , the subsequent analysis focuses primarily on the function interpolation.   Figure 2a demonstrates that the MHRBF achieves low error over range of € values; with the error 10-14 for all € 2 0.5, despite the fact that the condition number of the MHRBF being large",
